#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# wishart_matrix_distribution

#% text
# `wishart_matrix_distribution(nu, sigma)` is the distribution of the sum of `nu` outer products `x x^T` of independent vectors `x` of the multinormal distribution of covariance matrix `sigma`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The mean is `nu sigma` and the variance of the entry `[i, j]` is `nu (sigma[i][j]^2 + sigma[i][i] sigma[j][j])`.

#% item
# `pdf(d, x)` is the density at a positive definite matrix `x`.

#% item
# `random_variate(d)` draws a matrix as a sum of `nu` outer products of normal vectors (integer `nu` at least the dimension), `random_variate(d, n)` draws `n` of them.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mean(wishart_matrix_distribution(3, diagonal_matrix([2, 1, 3])))
#% output
#= [[6, 0, 0], [0, 3, 0], [0, 0, 9]]

#% cell
variance(wishart_matrix_distribution(3, diagonal_matrix([2, 1, 3])))
#% output
#= [[24, 6, 18], [6, 6, 9], [18, 9, 54]]

#% cell
pdf(wishart_matrix_distribution(3, [[1, 0], [0, 1]]), [[1, 0], [0, 1]])
#% output
#= 1/(4*e*pi)

#% cell
let w = random_variate(wishart_matrix_distribution(10, [[1, 1/3], [1/3, 1]])); [symmetric_matrix_q(w), positive_definite_matrix_q(w)]
#% output
#= [true, true]

